SUMMARY: Fire@Nite
DESCRIPTION:From 2 – 7 PM\n\nWitness performances throughout the museum i
 nvolving cast iron\, and be sure to hike the Trails to explore the variet
 y of sculptures in the museum’s collection.\n\nMeet the Trails Crew that 
 have traveled nation and worldwide to become an artist-in-residence at th
 e museum during the month of July.\n\nInterested in creating your very ow
 n cast iron art? Join us at our carving zone\, where the Sculpture Trails
  crew will be ready to help you make your own relief sculpture and cast i
 ron bowl during the event.\n\nFrom 8 – 10 PM\n\nStarting at 8 pm the main
  foundry will pour over 3\,000 pounds of cast iron using two large-scale 
 cast iron furnaces.\n\nWitness large metal sculptures being poured and pe
 rformance art done by artists from all over the world.\n\nCome on out and
  share this unique experience with us as our July Workshop comes to a fie
 ry close.\n\n\n*Disabled/accessible parking available near our foundry sp
 ace. Golf carts and disabled/accessible porta potties will be available*\
 n\n\nIf you have questions\, please contact us at lauravalentinag0225@gma
 il.com mailto:lauravalentinag0225@gmail.com or call (813) 808-5163. You c
 an also submit a contact form on our website!
CATEGORIES:Visual-Arts,In-Person,Free,Metal-Casting
